    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d844">

                <pb facs="0782" n="610" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg610"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 124.62/17a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d844-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-03T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 3, 1917, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>209. German Ambassador here, together with his staff, will be handed passport at
                    2 p.m. to-day. Immediately inform Spanish Government of this Government’s desire
                    that American interests in Germany may be cared for by the Spanish Embassy at
                    Berlin and request instructions be telegraphed there immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d844-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d844-f1-content">
                <p>See also telegram of Feb. 3 (No. 3860) to the Ambassador in Germany, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg585">p. 585</ref>.</p>
            </note>
